   "explanation": "360 = 2³ × 3² × 5. We need a × b × c = 360 with a ≤ b ≤ c and every side at least 6.\na = 6: b × c = 60 with 6 ≤ b ≤ c gives b = 6, c = 10 (b = 10 would need c = 6 < b).\na ≥ 7: 7 does not divide 360; a = 8 needs b × c = 45 with b ≥ 8, impossible (45 = 9 × 5); a = 9 needs b × c = 40 with b ≥ 9, impossible.\nSo the only cuboid is 6 by 6 by 10.",
   "answer": "6 cubes by 6 cubes by 10 cubes",
